  On the delivery of other integrations' changes: unconfined, all 4 of 4 arrive
  through EVENT_STATE_CHANGED, unasked and unfiltered. Confined, none arrive — but
  **in this run that is an absent feature, not a demonstrated filter**: this harness
  does not subscribe, so declared entities are mirrored once at construction and
  no state change has a path in. The filter itself is measured by selftest_push
  (§7.36, since 2026-10-04): declared changes delivered, undeclared ones not.
PASS — S3, both halves.
       Unconfined, the integration holds all 36 entities including every one of the
       20 that disclose presence, and is told about every change to entities it
       does not own.
       Confined, 6 of 6 undeclared probes are not in its state machine at all,
       every mediated read and subscription is refused with a clause, and the one
       entity it declared is readable.
       In this run the subscription half is a decision, not a delivered stream; the delivered,
       filtered stream is selftest_push's (§7.36) — see the note above.
